"example":"We need some food for the party.","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W01-example.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3"},{"id":"L5-W02","text":"drink","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W02.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3","example":"I’d like a drink, please.","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W02-example.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3"},{"id":"L5-W03","text":"furniture","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W03.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3","example":"There is new furniture in the living room.","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W03-example.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3"},{"id":"L5-W04","text":"clothing","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W04.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3","example":"This shop has clothing for men and women.","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W04-example.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3"},{"id":"L5-W05","text":"building","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W05.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3","example":"The library is an old building.","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W05-example.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3"},{"id":"L5-W06","text":"shop","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W06.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3","example":"There is a small shop near my house.","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l5/listen-repeat/L5-W06-example.mp3?v=20261003-sarah-slow1-r3"}]}},{"role":"practice","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L5-explanation-gaps","kind":"gaps","title":"Complete the sentences.","inputMode":"text","items":[{"id":"1","segments":["This beanbag is in the living room. It’s a ",{"id":"gap1","answers":["kind","type","sort"]}," of furniture."]},{"id":"2","segments":["I’d like bubble tea, please. It’s a ",{"id":"gap2","answers":["type","kind","sort"]}," of drink."]},{"id":"3","segments":["This poncho is warm and colorful. It’s a ",{"id":"gap3","answers":["sort","kind","type"]}," of clothing."]},{"id":"4","segments":["This igloo is small. It’s ",{"id":"gap4","answers":["like"]}," a little house."]},{"id":"5","segments":["Bao is food, but it looks different from the food I usually eat. It’s a ",{"id":"gap5","answers":["type","kind","sort"]}," of food."]},{"id":"6","segments":["There is a kiosk near the park. It’s ",{"id":"gap6","answers":["like"]}," a small supermarket."]}]}},{"role":"rule","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L5-kind-rule-homework-rule","kind":"rule-page","title":"Как объяснить незнакомую вещь","blocks":[{"type":"rule","text":"В английском языке незнакомую или необычную вещь можно объяснить двумя способами: сказать, к какой категории она относится, или сравнить её с чем-то знакомым.\n\n1. A kind of / a type of / a sort of\n\nИспользуйте a kind of, a type of или a sort of, чтобы сказать, к какой общей категории относится предмет.\n\nВ этом значении kind, type и sort означают практически одно и то же.\n\nIt’s a kind of furniture. — Это вид мебели.\nIt’s a type of drink. — Это вид напитка.\nIt’s a sort of building. — Это вид здания.\n\nПосле a kind of / a type of / a sort of называем общую категорию:\n\nfood · drink · furniture · clothing · building · shop\n\nОбратите внимание: в этой конструкции используется a:\n\na kind of · a type of · a sort of\n\n2. It’s like\n\nИспользуйте It’s like + noun, когда хотите сказать, на что похож предмет.\n\nIt’s like a big cushion. — Это похоже на большую подушку.\nIt’s like tea. — Это похоже на чай.\nIt’s like a small house. — Это похоже на маленький дом.\nIt’s like a bun. — Это похоже на булочку.\n\nСравните:\n\nIt’s a kind of furniture. — мы говорим, что это за категория.\nIt’s like a big cushion. — мы говорим, на что это похоже.\n\nТаким образом:\n\na kind of / a type of / a sort of → category\nlike → similarity","highlights":["A kind of / a type of / a sort of","a kind of","a type of","a sort of","It’s like","на что похож предмет","что это за категория","на что это похоже","like → similarity"]}]}},{"role":"translation","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L5-homework-1","kind":"writing","title":"Translate into English.","responseMode":"accepted","revealPossibleAnswers":false,"instruction":"Переведите вопросы и ответы на английский.","items":[{"id":"1","prompt":"На что похож бинбэг?","placeholder":"beanbag","acceptedAnswers":["What is a beanbag like?","What is a beanbag like","What''s a beanbag like?","What''s a beanbag like","What’s a beanbag like?","What’s a beanbag like"],"normalization":"translation"},{"id":"2","prompt":"Бинбэг — это вид мебели. Он похож на большую подушку.","placeholder":"beanbag","acceptedAnswers":["A beanbag is a kind of furniture. It is like a big cushion.","A beanbag is a kind of furniture. It is like a big cushion","A beanbag is a kind of furniture. It''s like a big cushion.","A beanbag is a kind of furniture. It''s like a big cushion","A beanbag is a kind of furniture. It’s like a big cushion.","A beanbag is a kind of furniture. It’s like a big cushion","A beanbag is a type of furniture. It is like a big cushion.","A beanbag is a type of furniture. It is like a big cushion","A beanbag is a type of furniture. It''s like a big cushion.","A beanbag is a type of furniture. It''s like a big cushion","A beanbag is a type of furniture