"audio","title":"Listen and repeat.","layout":"listen-repeat","audioPending":true,"items":[{"id":"L3_W01","text":"scarf","mediaRef":"L3_W01","example":"My scarf is on the chair.","exampleMediaRef":"L3_E01","audioId":"L3_W01","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_W01.mp3","exampleAudioId":"L3_E01","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_E01.mp3"},{"id":"L3_W02","text":"belt","mediaRef":"L3_W02","example":"Do you have a belt for these pants?","exampleMediaRef":"L3_E02","audioId":"L3_W02","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_W02.mp3","exampleAudioId":"L3_E02","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_E02.mp3"},{"id":"L3_W03","text":"gloves","mediaRef":"L3_W03","example":"I need my gloves. It’s cold.","exampleMediaRef":"L3_E03","audioId":"L3_W03","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_W03.mp3","exampleAudioId":"L3_E03","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_E03.mp3"},{"id":"L3_W04","text":"cap","mediaRef":"L3_W04","example":"Can you put my cap in the backpack, please?","exampleMediaRef":"L3_E04","audioId":"L3_W04","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_W04_r2.mp3?v=20260927-ready","exampleAudioId":"L3_E04","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_E04.mp3"},{"id":"L3_W05","text":"tie","mediaRef":"L3_W05","example":"My brother needs a tie for work.","exampleMediaRef":"L3_E05","audioId":"L3_W05","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_W05_tie-from-sentence-v2.wav?v=20260927-ready","exampleAudioId":"L3_E05","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_E05.mp3"},{"id":"L3_W06","text":"sunglasses","mediaRef":"L3_W06","example":"Where are my sunglasses? I need them today.","exampleMediaRef":"L3_E06","audioId":"L3_W06","audio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_W06.mp3","exampleAudioId":"L3_E06","exampleAudio":"https://xpeywyonbapnvtjnwawi.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/course-audio/a1-2/w4/l3/listen-repeat/L3_E06.mp3"}]}},{"role":"practice","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L4-question-answer-match","kind":"matching","title":"Match the questions with the answers.","items":[{"id":"1","text":"What is he like?","correctId":"o0"},{"id":"2","text":"What does she look like?","correctId":"o1"},{"id":"3","text":"What does he look like?","correctId":"o2"},{"id":"4","text":"What is she like?","correctId":"o3"}],"options":[{"id":"o1","text":"Her hair is short and curly."},{"id":"o0","text":"He’s a little lazy at home."},{"id":"o3","text":"She’s helpful. She often helps me with my homework."},{"id":"o2","text":"He has long straight hair."}]}},{"role":"practice","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L5-explanation-gaps","kind":"gaps","title":"Complete the sentences.","inputMode":"text","items":[{"id":"1","segments":["This beanbag is in the living room. It’s a ",{"id":"gap1","answers":["kind","type","sort"]}," of furniture."]},{"id":"2","segments":["I’d like bubble tea, please. It’s a ",{"id":"gap2","answers":["type","kind","sort"]}," of drink."]},{"id":"3","segments":["This poncho is warm and colorful. It’s a ",{"id":"gap3","answers":["sort","kind","type"]}," of clothing."]},{"id":"4","segments":["This igloo is small. It’s ",{"id":"gap4","answers":["like"]}," a little house."]},{"id":"5","segments":["Bao is food, but it looks different from the food I usually eat. It’s a ",{"id":"gap5","answers":["type","kind","sort"]}," of food."]},{"id":"6","segments":["There is a kiosk near the park. It’s ",{"id":"gap6","answers":["like"]}," a small supermarket."]}]}},{"role":"rule","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"a12w4l1-language-focus-homework-rule","kind":"rule-page","title":"Как описать внешний вид вещи","blocks":[{"type":"rule","title":"Как описать внешний вид вещи","text":"Когда вы хотите сказать, как выглядит вещь, используйте look / looks + прилагательное. Например, The sweater looks warm — «Свитер выглядит тёплым». Вы делитесь впечатлением по внешнему виду.\n\nЕсли вещь напоминает вам другую, используйте look / looks like + существительное или сочетание с ним: This coat looks like my old coat — «Это пальто похоже на моё старое пальто». Здесь like означает сходство, а не «нравится».\n\nСравните:\nIt looks good. — Мы описываем впечатление.\nIt looks like my coat. — Мы говорим, на что вещь похожа.\n\nФорма глагола зависит от того, о ком или о чём вы говорите:\nI / you / we / they → look\nhe / she / it → looks\n\nПоэтому об одном предмете говорим The coat looks good, а о нескольких — The coats look good.\n\nПосле like действуют знакомые правила артиклей: like a coat, like an old coat, но like my coat — перед my артикль не нужен.\n\nЧтобы спросить о внешнем впечатлении, используйте How does it look? — «Как это выглядит?» После does глагол look стоит без окончания -s.","highlights":["look / looks + прилагательное","The sweater looks warm","look / looks like + существительное или сочетание с ним","This coat looks like my old coat","like","It looks good.","It looks like my coat.","I / you / we / they → look","he / she / it → looks","The coat looks good","The coats look good","like a coat","like an old coat","like my coat","my","How does it look?","does","look","-s"]}]}},{"role":"rule","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L3-M07-rule-homework-rule","kind":"rule-page","title":"Как высказать мнение и объяснить причину","blocks":[{"type":"rule","title":"Как высказать мнение и объяснить причину","text":"Чтобы высказать своё мнение, используйте I think + предложение: I think these gloves look good — «Мне кажется, эти перчатки хорошо выглядят». После I think вы сообщаете свою мысль обычным предложением.\n\nСпросить мнение собеседника можно так: What do you think? — «Что вы думаете?» Например, в ответ можно сказать: I think it looks good.\n\nЕсли нужно объяснить выбор, добавьте because + предложение с причиной: I want this scarf because it’s warm — «Я хочу этот шарф, потому что он тёплый». В разговоре ответ на вопрос о причине может начинаться с because: Because it’s warm.","highlights":["I think + предложение","I think these gloves look good","I think","What do you think?","I think it looks good.","because + предложение с причиной","I want this scarf because it’s warm","because","Because it’s warm."]}]}},{"role":"rule","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L3-M08-explanation-homework-rule","kind":"rule-page","title":"Как спросить о выборе и причине","blocks":[{"type":"rule","title":"Как спросить о выборе и причине","text":"Когда перед вами несколько вариантов, which помогает спросить, какой из них выбирает человек: Which cap do you like? Если уже понятно, о какой вещи речь, можно сказать Which one do you like? Здесь one заменяет название одного предмета; после one повторять cap не нужно.\n\nО причине спрашиваем с why: Why do you like it? — «Почему вам это нравится?» Ответ объясняет причину: Because it looks good.\n\nПорядок вопроса знаком по Present Simple: Which/Why + do/does + подлежащее + глагол. Название предмета после which относится к вопросительной части: Which cap do you want? С he/she/it используем does, а основной глагол остаётся без -s: Why does she like it?\n\nЕсли говорим о нескольких предметах, называем их прямо: Which gloves do you like? В дальнейшем заменяем их на they/them: They look warm. Why do you like them?","highlights":["which","Which cap do you like?","Which one do you like?","one","cap","why","Why do you like it?","Because it looks good.","Which/Why + do/does + подлежащее + глагол","Which cap do you want?","he/she/it","does","-s","Why does she like it?","Which gloves do you like?","they/them","They look warm. Why do you like them?"]}]}},{"role":"rule","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L4-question-rule-homework-rule","kind":"rule-page","title":"Как спросить о человеке","blocks":[{"type":"rule","text":"В английском языке вопросы What is he/she like? и What does he/she look like? используются, когда мы хотим узнать разную информацию о человеке.\n\n1. What is he/she like?\n\nИспользуйте What is he/she like?, чтобы спросить, какой человек по характеру или поведению.\n\nWhat is she like? — Какая она?\nShe is polite and helpful. — Она вежливая и готовая помочь.\n\nВ ответе используйте be + adjective:\n\nHe is quiet.\nShe is rude.\n\n2. What does he/she look like?\n\nИспользуйте What does he/she look like?, чтобы спросить, как человек выглядит.\n\nWhat does she look like? — Как она выглядит?\nShe has long brown hair. — У неё длинные каштановые волосы.\n\nДля описания внешности можно использовать have/has + noun:\n\nHe has short straight hair.\nShe has long curly hair.\n\n3. What does he/she like?\n\nНе путайте What is she like? и What does she like?\n\nWhat does she like? означает «Что ей нравится?»\n\nWhat does she like? — Что ей нравится?\nShe likes music. — Ей нравится музыка.","highlights":["What is he/she like?","What does he/she look like?","What does he/she like?","What is she like?","What does she look like?","What does she like?","be + adjective","have/has + noun"]}]}},{"role":"rule","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L5-kind-rule-homework-rule","kind":"rule-page","title":"Как объяснить незнакомую вещь","blocks":[{"type":"rule","text":"В английском языке незнакомую или необычную вещь можно объяснить двумя способами: сказать, к какой категории она относится, или сравнить её с чем-то знакомым.\n\n1. A kind of / a type of / a sort of\n\nИспользуйте a kind of, a type of или a sort of, чтобы сказать, к какой общей категории относится предмет.\n\nВ этом значении kind, type и sort означают практически одно и то же.\n\nIt’s a kind of furniture. — Это вид мебели.\nIt’s a type of drink. — Это вид напитка.\nIt’s a sort of building. — Это вид здания.\n\nПосле a kind of / a type of / a sort of называем общую категорию:\n\nfood · drink · furniture · clothing · building · shop\n\nОбратите внимание: в этой конструкции используется a:\n\na kind of · a type of · a sort of\n\n2. It’s like\n\nИспользуйте It’s like + noun, когда хотите сказать, на что похож предмет.\n\nIt’s like a big cushion. — Это похоже на большую подушку.\nIt’s like tea. — Это похоже на чай.\nIt’s like a small house. — Это похоже на маленький дом.\nIt’s like a bun. — Это похоже на булочку.\n\nСравните:\n\nIt’s a kind of furniture. — мы говорим, что это за категория.\nIt’s like a big cushion. — мы говорим, на что это похоже.\n\nТаким образом:\n\na kind of / a type of / a sort of → category\nlike → similarity","highlights":["A kind of / a type of / a sort of","a kind of","a type of","a sort of","It’s like","на что похож предмет","что это за категория","на что это похоже","like → similarity"]}]}},{"role":"translation","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L6-homework-1","kind":"writing","title":"Translate into English.","instruction":"Переведите на английский.","responseMode":"accepted","revealPossibleAnswers":false,"items":[{"id":"1","prompt":"Как смотрятся эти свитеры?","acceptedAnswers":["How do these sweaters look?","How do these sweaters look"],"normalization":"translation"},{"id":"2","prompt":"Они действительно красивые.","acceptedAnswers":["They are really beautiful.","They are really pretty.","they''re really beautiful.","they''re really pretty.","They are really beautiful","They are really pretty","they’re really beautiful.","they''re really beautiful","they’re really pretty.","they''re really pretty"],"normalization":"translation"},{"id":"3","prompt":"То пальто похоже на платье.","acceptedAnswers":["That coat looks like a dress.","That coat looks like a dress"],"normalization":"translation"},{"id":"4","prompt":"Эти шляпы немного странные.","acceptedAnswers":["These hats are a little strange.","These hats are a bit strange.","These hats are a little strange","These hats are a bit strange"],"normalization":"translation"},{"id":"5","prompt":"Какие тебе нравятся: эти перчатки или те?","acceptedAnswers":["Which ones do you like: these gloves or those?","Which ones do you like: these gloves or those ones?","Which gloves do you like: these or those?","Which ones do you like: these gloves or those","Which ones do you like these gloves or those","Which ones do you like: these gloves or those ones","Which ones do you like these gloves or those ones","Which gloves do you like: these or those","Which gloves do you like these or those"],"normalization":"translation"},{"id":"6","prompt":"Мне нравятся те, потому что они тёмные.","acceptedAnswers":["I like those because they are dark.","I like those ones because they are dark.","I like those because they''re dark.","I like those ones because they''re dark.","I like those because they are dark","I like those ones because they are dark","I like those because they’re dark.","I like those because they''re dark","I like those ones because they’re dark.","I like those ones because they''re dark"],"normalization":"translation"}]}},{"role":"translation","exercise":{"version":1,"id":"L6-homework-2","kind":"writing","title":"Translate into English.","instruction":"Переведите на английский.","responseMode":"accepted","revealPossibleAnswers":false,"items":[{"id":"1","prompt":"Этот костюм слишком яркий.","acceptedAnswers":["This suit is too bright.","This suit''s too bright.","This suit is too bright","This suit’s too bright.","This suit''s too bright"],"normalization":"translation"},{"id":"2","prompt":"Та юбка такая красивая!","acceptedAnswers":["That skirt